{# THE SIDEBAR'S SHAPE — sections, rows, and the location tree.

   The shell owns every line of this drawing and not one word in it. Sections and
   rows arrive as data from the tagged sources; whatever a source hands over is
   what renders, and no name is ever recognised.

   ONE LINE GRAMMAR, APPLIED AT EVERY DEPTH: a rail drops out of the bottom of a
   parent row at that parent's content centre and ticks sideways into each child.
   The indent steps once per level and the rail always sits at the previous
   level's centre, which is what makes the levels read as one drawing rather than
   three lists.

   FOLDING IS A CLASS, NEVER AN OMISSION. A caret that folds by not rendering its
   children has nothing to reopen, and the row becomes a one-way door. Children
   are always in the document; `closed` hides them. #}
<nav class="nav" data-controller="uhifadhi--shell-bundle--sidebar-tree">
    {% for section in sections %}
        <div class="nav-hd">{{ section.label }}</div>
        {% for item in section.items %}
            {{ include('@Shell/_nav_item.html.twig', {item: item, depth: 1}, with_context: false) }}
        {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
</nav>
